:db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42662" :question/id #uuid "d27e1410-6d2c-5849-b4f0-5d86e8924bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42662" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/e2f149fb4f32fb264e0af6898e7737d570ec90bbff31cf1256eb9bd2636ceab3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $w=\\lambda u+\\mu v$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/589f9f524a7c98da61ad6c5001b8d392d89073d5734cd70cfa750d153fe6f7b7.png)\n\nIn $△OUW$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OU=2|v|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OU}$ has the opposite direction to $v$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=-2v.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $UW=4|u|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{UW}$ has the opposite direction to $u$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{UW}=-4u.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =-2v-4u \\\\  & =-4u-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $w=\\lambda u+\\mu v=-4u-2v.$\n\nSince $u∦v,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42662/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-120285"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/c4d26b3db6446f586ca47634d9f9a3a004968a0081b8859ce46b4b4af799d066.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=i$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=3:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-275128/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "79faca23-cc2f-5c5c-b789-a9e286ea99d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275128/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "4f0a43bc-5415-59c2-a9a7-0ed10cb2c862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275128/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b100796-ab8c-5829-b7c0-21c5b307092c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275128/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-275128/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-275128/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275128/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "9b703e0c-1828-55e5-be16-9b8fa50851e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275128/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "90b4534a-4d56-520e-9cbd-ca4ad433ac7c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275128/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-275128/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275128" :question/id #uuid "9bf2d1d7-06cd-5a1b-a4ab-399010ca0c3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275128" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/992be4e67316804381ffc38860d2eaf23fd4a93cfe22ec4918c30c41e34ade57.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/c0f7f4df52373ca602aff41c97a5b8413f510353874540b76147c527a2f4b18c.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=\\frac{1}{2}|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-\\frac{1}{2}r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=\\frac{5}{2}|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-\\frac{5}{2}s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{5}{2}$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275128/field-1" "q-275128/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275128"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290/selection/8cf44f693cb1ac41b425913c9b85ecb009760a83be7a3f54bff5a21832797a1e" :answer/id #uuid "bda315af-ccc9-53c8-9453-fbb1972c8fa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{8}{13}f+\\frac{5}{13}g" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290/selection/3554a90eb0d322136d78452db9a414a6ef438c594f13b9d29d78d2209df36004" :answer/id #uuid "ab12ad40-40b5-5bee-9964-a8d64a04e9d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290/selection/94a2820d3f56abe88ca0e7696cb889aa7bae651e17d4f695b919a9404a442181" :answer/id #uuid "76bea49f-dc71-5058-a5c5-11161bb656b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=f+\\frac{8}{5}g" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290/selection/8ea20d0d15ac956c7b11af29c653d1edcd931952f23ce7c020ce9e51cb2fa094" :answer/id #uuid "c29743d4-d73f-5449-b4b1-5bffab50d228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{8}f+\\frac{1}{5}g" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290/selection/3f71ba1f84e1f0c6e02bb61aad4808fd17cb6c56336af1e3591937eb659509ae" :answer/id #uuid "2d7d3a0c-e7f6-5a55-bf81-aa2123fac05b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{8}f+\\frac{1}{8}g" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56048438-df7a-5832-ac34-4fcc26be6ddf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-278290/selection/3554a90eb0d322136d78452db9a414a6ef438c594f13b9d29d78d2209df36004" :answer-field/choices ["q-278290/selection/8cf44f693cb1ac41b425913c9b85ecb009760a83be7a3f54bff5a21832797a1e" "q-278290/selection/3554a90eb0d322136d78452db9a414a6ef438c594f13b9d29d78d2209df36004" "q-278290/selection/94a2820d3f56abe88ca0e7696cb889aa7bae651e17d4f695b919a9404a442181" "q-278290/selection/8ea20d0d15ac956c7b11af29c653d1edcd931952f23ce7c020ce9e51cb2fa094" "q-278290/selection/3f71ba1f84e1f0c6e02bb61aad4808fd17cb6c56336af1e3591937eb659509ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278290" :question/id #uuid "cb79b649-cc96-59ab-927e-8bb7778fa82d" :question/math-academy-id "q-278290" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/36aeda6b6f5ce46552f55f458da60ef46a646d737c452d586389c03c47d1c9cb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g$ and $P$ divides $\\overset{―}{FG}$ in the ratio $FP:PG=8:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{FP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OFG,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =\\overset{\\to }{FO}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-f+g \\\\  & =g-f.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $FP:PG=8:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{FP}=\\frac{8}{13}\\overset{\\to }{FG}=\\frac{8}{13}(g-f).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP} \\\\  & =f+\\frac{8}{13}(g-f) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322574/field-1/ff0685038436a148f4cbd816798fad7bc9dca49bd0c36c3225582ac51388eb1d" :answer/id #uuid "8af4c36e-bab6-59d8-baec-35aea10345a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322574/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6da47429-f7d2-5907-b203-fe3a3ba45214" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322574/field-1/ff0685038436a148f4cbd816798fad7bc9dca49bd0c36c3225582ac51388eb1d" :answer-field/choices ["q-322574/field-1/ff0685038436a148f4cbd816798fad7bc9dca49bd0c36c3225582ac51388eb1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322574/field-2/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c" :answer/id #uuid "95cace35-39ca-5f5e-a7e0-d26cc53e39c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322574/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8304a8c-d3e7-59e7-aeca-7e8a7a4fbd1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322574/field-2/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c" :answer-field/choices ["q-322574/field-2/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322574" :question/id #uuid "6455512b-935f-5f04-b876-901ffd05fe90" :question/math-academy-id "q-322574" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/2a9cacfc6787e60229076c4abd2854709d51ac718c8d519256a61dbe92852b05.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{GH}$ in the ratio $GJ:JH=6:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}$ via the vectors $g$ and $h.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$g+$\n{{field-2}}\n$h$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{GJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{GJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OGH,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GH} & =\\overset{\\to }{GO}+\\overset{\\to }{OH} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{OH} \\\\  & =-g+h \\\\  & =h-g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $GJ:JH=6:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{GJ}=\\frac{6}{13}\\overset{\\to }{GH}=\\frac{6}{13}(h-g).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{GJ} \\\\  & =g+\\frac{6}{13}(h-g) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}g+\\frac{6}{13}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322574/field-1" "q-322574/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
